     [38;2;248;248;242m[2m   [22m onto a map showing where you are, your nearest Metrobus stop and, eventually, where the buses are, so a rider can glance at a phone and decide when to leave. The ma[2m[6;7H [22m[1Cin user is[1Cthe owner, a[1Cregular rider using[1Cit one-handed on[1Ca [1Chone before[1Cheading out, and[1Cany other rider uses[1Cit an[1Cnymously with nothing to set up. There is no [7;9Hexisting frontend, so this sets the visual language from[2Ccratch. It sho[1Cld feel calm, glanc[1Cable and util[1Cta[1Cian:[1Cthe map fills th[2Cscreen and[1Cev[1Cry[1Ching else is[2Ci[8;9Hnimal floating[1Cchrome[1Cwith large touch tar[1Cets[1Cnear the bottom[1Cfor thumb [2Cach. Use[1Ca cle[2C system sans-serif [1Ctack,[2C light, muted map base,[1Cand a restrained[1Cpalett[9;9Hor the use[1C's locati[1Cn dot[1Cand accuracy halo, and a[1Cdistin[1Ct highlighted mark[1Cr for the near[1Cst stop.[1CAny bus d[1Cta[1Ccarries[1Ca small but cl[1Carly visible "sch[1Cduled"[1Cba[10;9Hdge because it[1Cis estima[1Ced f[1Com[2Che timetable[1Cand must[1Cnever lo[1Ck[1Clive.[1COpenStreetM[1Cp attribution[1Cis always visible[1Cin a map[1Ccorner. Design the phon[1C f[2Cmes at 390 [11;9Hby[1C844, plus one desktop fr[1Cme[1Cof the map scree[1C to[1Cshow that [1Ct scales responsively. The fir[4Ccreen is[1Cthe[1CM[1Cp home screen: [1C full-s[1Cr[1Cen map centred on the user'[12;9Hs blu[1C locat[1Con dot and zoomed so tha[1C the nearest[1Cstop[1C(and the nearest[1Cbus, if one is shown) [1Cs in vie[1C. The near[1Cst stop is highlighted wi[2C its [1Came [1Cnd the[1Cline[13;9Hs that serve[1Cit in a c[1Cmpact bottom card                                                                                                                                    [38;2;153;153;153m[14;6H… +4 lines                                                                                                                   